   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "PALM GAP FOR CLAPS\n\ngap = ‖centre_a − centre_b‖ / ½(scale_a + scale_b)   metres\n\nNothing is heard. Hands that meet are often read as one hand or none,\nso palms that vanish on their way together count as having met. A\nswipe is suppressed while the palms are within 0.35 m, or within 700\nms of meeting.",
   "originalText": "PALM GAP FOR CLAPS\n\ngap = ‖centre_a − centre_b‖ / ½(scale_a + scale_b)   metres\n\nNothing is heard. Hands that meet are often read as one hand or none, so palms that vanish on their way together count as having met. A swipe is suppressed while the palms are within 0.35 m, or within 700 ms of meeting.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "ht0751",
   "lineHeight": 1.2,
   "autoResize": true
  },
